OL,3,GNEWSAPSNI taking 'more robust' approach
OL,4,Ato e-bikes and scooters
OL,5,
OL,6,FE-Scooters and e-bikes have "become a
OL,7,Fchallenging issue" for the Police
OL,8,FService of Northern Ireland (PSNI), the
OL,9,Flead road safety officer has said.
OL,11,FFrom 1 January until 31 October 2026
OL,12,Fprovisional figures show 473 of the
OL,13,Fmachines were seized by the PSNI, 379
OL,14,Fof which were e-scooters.
OL,16,FIn the two years between 1 September
OL,17,F2024 and 31 August 2026, provisional
OL,18,Fpolice figures also show there were 150
OL,19,Fcollisions involving e-scooters
OL,20,Freported to the PSNI. There were two
OL,21,Ffatalities in that time and 45 people
OL,22,Fsustained serious injuries.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
